Subject: [PATCH 0/3] arm: tighten feature selection and inference paths

This series contains three independently reviewable corrections found while
validating llama.cpp on native aarch64:

  1. Select KleidiAI Arm sources from the final compile-probe results instead
     of feature-name substrings in -march.
  2. Replace 32 scalar byte stores in the NEON Q8_0 quantizer with in-register
     narrowing and two vector stores.
  3. Prevent unrelated generation-prompt tokens from advancing the forced
     reasoning-end sequence, with a focused regression test.

The patches are kept separate because their mechanisms and correctness
obligations differ. They are grouped here only as the exact b10216 series used
by the Arm service validation; each commit can be reviewed independently.

Existing native aarch64 evidence for this exact source diff includes clean
application, the upstream quantizer and reasoning tests, reproduction of the
invalid SVE-source selection before the feature fix, emitted-assembly checks,
and a complete Arm CPU build followed by all 47 tests in the upstream main
label. A separate local validation contract records GCC, Clang, and targeted
ASan/UBSan results without changing these patches.

Arshdeep Singh (3):
  ggml-cpu: select KleidiAI sources from feature probes
  ggml-cpu: use vector stores in quantize_row_q8_0
  common: guard forced reasoning-token acceptance

